WebGL: BC4, BC5, BC6H and BC7 with the RGTC and BPTC extensions

On Emscripten every texture format is checked against the WebGL extensions it needs (isTextureFormatValidPerSpec),
and BC4, BC5, BC6H, BC6HU and BC7 fell through to the default case, so they were never supported in the browser
even where the context offers EXT_texture_compression_rgtc and EXT_texture_compression_bptc, which nearly every
browser that offers WEBGL_compressed_texture_s3tc offers too. BC4 and BC5 already switch to the RGTC formats when
the extension is listed, and the BPTC formats are the ones WebGL's extension takes, so only the check was missing.
BC4, BC5 and BC6H have no sRGB form; BC7 has one in EXT_texture_compression_bptc.

diff --git a/src/renderer_gl.cpp b/src/renderer_gl.cpp
--- a/src/renderer_gl.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_gl.cpp
@@ -1748,6 +1748,21 @@ namespace bgfx { namespace gl
 					&& (!_srgb || emscripten_webgl_enable_extension(ctx, "WEBGL_compressed_texture_s3tc_srgb") )
 					;
 
+			case TextureFormat::BC4:
+			case TextureFormat::BC5:
+				return !_srgb
+					&& emscripten_webgl_enable_extension(ctx, "EXT_texture_compression_rgtc")
+					;
+
+			case TextureFormat::BC6H:
+			case TextureFormat::BC6HU:
+				return !_srgb
+					&& emscripten_webgl_enable_extension(ctx, "EXT_texture_compression_bptc")
+					;
+
+			case TextureFormat::BC7:
+				return emscripten_webgl_enable_extension(ctx, "EXT_texture_compression_bptc");
+
 			case TextureFormat::PTC12:
 			case TextureFormat::PTC14:
 			case TextureFormat::PTC12A:
